# Root-level .dockerignore (2026-10-01) -- only exists because the
# `frontend` service's build context was widened from ./frontend-react to
# the repo root (see docker-compose.yml's comment), so DocumentationPage.tsx
# can reach ../../../docs/*.md?raw at build time. Without this file, every
# frontend build would send the ENTIRE repo to the builder -- notably
# data/ (500MB+ of bind-mounted Postgres/Redis/media state) and .git/ --
# instead of just the ~2 directories that build actually needs.
#
# "Exclude everything, then re-include only what's needed" -- the other
# three services (backend-django, backend-go, backend-node) each keep
# their OWN .dockerignore scoped to their own build context and are
# unaffected by this file, since Docker only reads the .dockerignore at
# the build context root being used for that particular build.
**
!frontend-react
!frontend-react/**
!docs
!docs/**
frontend-react/node_modules
frontend-react/node_modules/**
frontend-react/dist
frontend-react/dist/**
frontend-react/.env
